x-versions-release-field.md (11 numbered decisions plus Evidence and Consequences); docs/adr/README.md and docs/adr/.numbers/0123 come from scripts/gen_adr_index.py.\n- scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check: exit 0. scripts/check_adr_numbers.py: exit 0. rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD: OK.\n- make verify (JIRA_URL/JIRA_USER/JIRA_API_TOKEN unset), 13:52-14:46 PST: exit 0. Default tier 20847 passed, 29 skipped; integration tier 202 passed, 2 skipped.\n- Pushed as Gerrit change 3337, WIP, hashtag rebar-session-a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d. HOLD: this epic must not land in release 0.14.1; the change stays WIP until the operator posts RELEASED, then lands at LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / 0 unresolved comments.\n- The ticket closes only after 3337 merges.","timestamp":1794264476616419001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR number collision 2026-11-09 (PST): another session's worktree adr-0123-plan-engine holds commit 93a8eea0870 adding docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md (ticket 11f7-cf57-be02-4441), while Gerrit change 3337 had also claimed 0123. Change 3337 is held until release 0.14.1 is cut, so it yields: the fix-versions ADR is renumbered to 0124 (free on main, every local branch and worktree, and open Gerrit changes at the time of the check). Child ticket descriptions now cite ADR 0124; earlier comments citing ADR 0123 for this design mean ADR 0124.","timestamp":1794264779639864001}],"created_at":1794256363092640001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"354c0ae9-1f8b-4544-8a0e-d6d62d4813f0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fffe-887d-67cd-4901"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas` makes release a first-class rebar ticket field synced both ways with Jira's `fixVersions`. Its approach step 1 requires an ADR before any code, so the later children (reducer, inbound, outbound, missing-version alert, surfaces) build against one recorded design. The operator settled the product decisions on 2026-11-05 (epic description and comments). This ADR records them and settles what the epic delegates to it: the replayed event carrier, the field name, the `FIELD_CONTRACT` class, name identity and renames, and archived/deleted versions.\n\n## Approach\n\nWrite `docs/adr/0124-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` (next free number: the last marker is `docs/adr/.numbers/0122`; 0123 is taken by the selectable plan-review engine ADR (ticket `11f7-cf57-be02-4441`), and 0124 is free on main, local branches and open Gerrit changes on 2026-11-09) with a `## Decision` section of numbered items:\n\n1. **Field shape.** Compiled state gains `releases`: a list of Jira version names, default `[]`, insertion-ordered, no duplicates. Names only: no release records, status or dates.\n2. **Carrier.** A new event `RELEASE_DELTA {\"added\", \"removed\", \"source\"?}` folded by `process_release_delta` with `process_tag_delta`'s rules (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:429-449`): removals first, then additions. Rejected: a field selector on `TAG_DELTA`, because an older clone that knows `TAG_DELTA` would fold release names into `tags`; a new type takes the preserve-and-ignore path for unknown types (`src/rebar/reducer/_version.py:8-16`). `SCHEMA_VERSION` 5 → 6, readers before writers (reconcile host first), as `docs/event-schema.md` prescribes for a new body type.\n3. **Symmetry.** `FIELD_CONTRACT[\"releases\"]`: `ADD_WINS`, conflict class `set`, `outbound_name=\"fixVersions\"`, like `labels` (`src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py:108-119`); `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES[\"releases\"] = \"set\"`.\n4. **Inbound.** Set-diff Jira `fixVersions[].name` against `releases` like `_diff_labels_inbound` (`src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py:194-214`); write `RELEASE_DELTA` with `source=\"inbound\"`, suppressing no-ops and skipping the write when the reducer fails, like `_inbound_update_apply_labels` (`src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py:322-389`). An unobserved `fixVersions` key yields no diff.\n5. **Outbound.** ADD names the issue lacks; REMOVE only names in the local ever-seen intent set (non-inbound `RELEASE_DELTA.added` and `SNAPSHOT` releases), mirroring the intent gate in `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_labels.py:43-85`. Per-item verbs only: Cloud `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/{key}` with `{\"update\":{\"fixVersions\":[{\"add\":{\"name\":N}}]}}` or `remove`; Data Center `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\":[...]})`, the verb the DC label remove uses (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:196`). Never `set`.\n6. **Same pass.** Outbound wins: the suppression in `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py:298-322` (which drops an inbound REMOVE of a name in the outbound context's adds, and vice versa) is extended to releases, and the outbound context for releases records both emitted ADDs and ADDs withheld under item 8.\n7. **Identity and renames.** The name is the identity (Jira Cloud OpenAPI `Version.name`: unique per project). A rename of a Jira-originated release surfaces as remove old plus add new. A rebar-set name that a rename or deletion makes stop existing is withheld under item 8; because item 6 records withheld ADDs in the outbound context, the inbound REMOVE of the old name is suppressed, so the old name stays with an alert and, after a rename, the new name also arrives inbound. Recorded as a consequence.\n8. **Missing version.** Read each bound project's versions once per pass (Cloud `GET /rest/api/3/project/{key}/versions`; DC `project_versions`). Withhold an ADD the project lacks (no Jira write, but recorded as an outbound add for item 6), keep the name, write one `BRIDGE_ALERT` per (ticket, name) with reason `release-version-missing:<name>`, retry every pass, and resolve the alert when the name is no longer withheld. An unreadable version list means unknown: no alert, no resolution. The bridge never creates versions.\n9. **Archived and deleted.** Withhold an archived version like a missing one (reason `release-version-archived:<name>`): Jira's behavior on adding one is unverified (no version exists on the site, and the Atlassian pages checked on 2026-11-09 do not state it), and withholding cannot write an unexpected value. Archived names on an issue still sync inbound; their REMOVE is attempted. A deleted version is absent, so item 8 applies; when Jira strips it from issues, inbound removes it.\n10. **Out of scope.** Affects versions (`versions`); parent inheritance (`list --release X` returns exactly tickets whose own `releases` hold X); any config key.\n11. **Surfaces.** `rebar edit --add-release/--remove-release/--set-releases` (set is an add-wins delta like `--set-tags`), `rebar list --release`, `rebar show`, library `edit_ticket` keywords `add_releases`/`remove_releases`/`set_releases` and `list_tickets(release=)`, and the derived MCP parameters and read `outputSchema`s.\n\nAn `## Evidence` section records the read-only Jira checks of 2026-11-09 (PST), each with its endpoint: the `fixVersions` field schema (`/rest/api/3/field`); REB-7015 editmeta without `fixVersions`; 0 versions in all 144 visible projects and 0 issues matching `fixVersion is not EMPTY`; Atlassian's documented Set/Add/Remove support for Fix Versions; and the edit endpoint's statement that it \"doesn't check screen configurations\", which contradicts the epic's REB edit-screen prerequisite and is left for the production-verification child to settle live.\n\nThen run `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py`, which derives both `docs/adr/README.md` (a generated file; the slug's `jira` keyword files it under \"Reconciler & Jira sync\", `scripts/gen_adr_index.py:69-73`) and the marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0124`. Neither is edited by hand.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/0124-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` (new)\n- `docs/adr/.numbers/0124` (generated marker)\n- `docs/adr/README.md` (regenerated index)\n\nDocumentation only: no code, no new testable behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0124-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` has `**Status:** Accepted` and a `## Decision` section with one numbered item for each of the 11 Approach points.\n- [ ] Decision item 2 names the rejected `TAG_DELTA` field selector with its older-clone corruption reason.\n- [ ] Decision item 2 records `SCHEMA_VERSION` 6 with readers-before-writers rollout.\n- [ ] The `## Evidence` section lists the 5 read-only findings, each with its endpoint or source.\n- [ ] The `## Evidence` section names the edit-screen contradiction.\n- [ ] Decision items 6 and 8 both state that a withheld ADD is recorded in the outbound context, and item 7's rename consequence cites that rule.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0 with `docs/adr/.numbers/0124` present.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/README.md` links `0124-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md` under \"Reconciler & Jira sync\".\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0123-jira-fix-versions-release-field.md","reason":"new ADR"},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0123","reason":"ADR number marker"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"index entry"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"],["relates_to","fffe-887d-67cd-4901"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"4d2c09e6-7d8a-4c6b-ad2f-1af7a05e19e9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0f4c-4586-8f3e-432d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Record the release-field design for Jira fix versions in ADR 0123","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["896a12a3-9916-4800-9ede-257f34fe6d58","1c560690-8f12-4651-90f0-98409958c9d0","218f212e-2685-469c-8abc-fd6a8d173806","52e245cd-a050-4df6-8fbd-d68b87fb7496","068001ec-1cfa-4c2e-a124-c9b5f9a8e0bc","0d6673ea-87b5-40e5-a8ca-dec699d8cca0","4d2c09e6-7d8a-4c6b-ad2f-1af7a05e19e9","f643562b-8e9a-4d11-b64a-23d4126a297b","0f43a028-2d4f-4ab0-8ce9-d39269ee527b","9cc4c9ba-d5c9-49c4-8514-c859c7b13d4e","354c0ae9-1f8b-4544-8a0e-d6d62d4813f0","f0860f56-d8df-45e7-8bfe-df72000c8961"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794264779639864002,"uuid":"5c86d0bf-7ce2-465b-9ff2-077cc3e65ddd"}